1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:15,419
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June eighteenth. The Bank of Japan has raised its interest rate to one percent — something we haven't seen in a very long time. Let's listen.

2
00:00:16,019 --> 00:00:18,780
[News] 今日のニュースです。

3
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:25,263
[News] 日本銀行が、金利を1%に上げました。

4
00:00:25,963 --> 00:00:32,780
[News] 金利は、お金を借りるときにはらう、お金の値段のことです。

5
00:00:33,479 --> 00:00:39,408
[News] 金利が1%になるのは、とても久しぶりです。

6
00:00:40,107 --> 00:00:45,531
[News] 最近、いろいろな物の値段が高くなっています。

7
00:00:46,231 --> 00:00:52,256
[News] それで、日本銀行は金利を上げることにしました。

8
00:00:52,956 --> 00:01:01,283
[News] 金利が上がると、銀行に貯金している人は、もらえるお金が少し増えます。

9
00:01:01,984 --> 00:01:07,936
[News] でも、お金を借りている人は、返すお金が増えます。

10
00:01:08,635 --> 00:01:16,628
[News] 家を買うためにお金を借りた家庭は、毎月のお金が増えるかもしれません。

11
00:01:17,328 --> 00:01:24,096
[News] これから、私たちの生活がどうなるか、みんなが見ています。

12
00:01:24,796 --> 00:01:26,427
[Host] Let's break it down.

13
00:01:27,028 --> 00:01:33,628
[Slow] 日本銀行が、金利を1%に上げました。

14
00:01:34,427 --> 00:01:38,268
[Host] The Bank of Japan raised its interest rate to one percent.

15
00:01:38,867 --> 00:01:41,004
[Vocab] 金利

16
00:01:41,403 --> 00:01:49,540
[Host] It means the interest rate — the cost of borrowing money, given as a percentage. A higher rate means costlier loans.

17
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:57,939
[Slow] 金利は、お金を借りるときにはらう、お金の値段のことです。

18
00:01:58,739 --> 00:02:02,748
[Host] The interest rate is the price of money — what you pay when you borrow.

19
00:02:03,347 --> 00:02:05,507
[Vocab] 借りる

20
00:02:05,908 --> 00:02:12,891
[Host] It means to borrow. Its partner word is to lend: you borrow from the bank, and the bank lends to you.

21
00:02:13,491 --> 00:02:20,259
[Slow] 金利が1%になるのは、とても久しぶりです。

22
00:02:21,060 --> 00:02:24,804
[Host] It has been a very long time since the rate was at one percent.

23
00:02:25,403 --> 00:02:27,948
[Vocab] 久しぶり

24
00:02:28,348 --> 00:02:34,852
[Host] It means after a long time. You'll also hear it as a greeting — the equivalent of 'long time no see.'

25
00:02:35,451 --> 00:02:41,668
[Slow] 最近、いろいろな物の値段が高くなっています。

26
00:02:42,467 --> 00:02:46,331
[Host] Lately, the prices of all kinds of things have been going up.

27
00:02:46,931 --> 00:02:49,020
[Vocab] 値段

28
00:02:49,419 --> 00:02:55,683
[Host] It means price — how much something costs. You'll see this word on every shelf and menu.

29
00:02:56,283 --> 00:03:03,147
[Slow] それで、日本銀行は金利を上げることにしました。

30
00:03:03,948 --> 00:03:07,331
[Host] So the Bank of Japan decided to raise the rate.

31
00:03:07,931 --> 00:03:10,068
[Vocab] 上げる

32
00:03:10,467 --> 00:03:19,180
[Host] It means to raise or lift something up. Here the bank raises the rate. The partner verb, to go up on its own, is a different word.

33
00:03:19,780 --> 00:03:29,283
[Slow] 金利が上がると、銀行に貯金している人は、もらえるお金が少し増えます。

34
00:03:30,084 --> 00:03:35,027
[Host] When the rate goes up, people who keep savings at the bank earn a little more.

35
00:03:35,627 --> 00:03:37,812
[Vocab] 貯金

36
00:03:38,211 --> 00:03:44,620
[Host] It means savings — money you keep in the bank. The two characters together mean 'store up money.'

37
00:03:45,219 --> 00:03:52,012
[Slow] でも、お金を借りている人は、返すお金が増えます。

38
00:03:52,812 --> 00:03:56,075
[Host] But people who have borrowed money now have more to pay back.

39
00:03:56,675 --> 00:03:58,979
[Vocab] 返す

40
00:03:59,379 --> 00:04:05,883
[Host] It means to return something or pay it back — return a borrowed book, or pay back borrowed money.

41
00:04:06,484 --> 00:04:15,604
[Slow] 家を買うためにお金を借りた家庭は、毎月のお金が増えるかもしれません。

42
00:04:16,403 --> 00:04:20,771
[Host] Households that borrowed money to buy a home might pay more each month.

43
00:04:21,372 --> 00:04:23,555
[Vocab] 増える

44
00:04:23,956 --> 00:04:29,668
[Host] It means to increase — to grow in number or amount. The opposite is to decrease.

45
00:04:30,267 --> 00:04:33,267
[Host] Let's listen to the full story one more time.

46
00:04:33,867 --> 00:04:36,627
[News] 今日のニュースです。

47
00:04:37,327 --> 00:04:43,112
[News] 日本銀行が、金利を1%に上げました。

48
00:04:43,812 --> 00:04:50,627
[News] 金利は、お金を借りるときにはらう、お金の値段のことです。

49
00:04:51,327 --> 00:04:57,255
[News] 金利が1%になるのは、とても久しぶりです。

50
00:04:57,956 --> 00:05:03,379
[News] 最近、いろいろな物の値段が高くなっています。

51
00:05:04,079 --> 00:05:10,103
[News] それで、日本銀行は金利を上げることにしました。

52
00:05:10,803 --> 00:05:19,132
[News] 金利が上がると、銀行に貯金している人は、もらえるお金が少し増えます。

53
00:05:19,831 --> 00:05:25,783
[News] でも、お金を借りている人は、返すお金が増えます。

54
00:05:26,483 --> 00:05:34,475
[News] 家を買うためにお金を借りた家庭は、毎月のお金が増えるかもしれません。

55
00:05:35,175 --> 00:05:41,944
[News] これから、私たちの生活がどうなるか、みんなが見ています。

56
00:05:42,644 --> 00:05:45,379
[Host] Quiz time. Three questions.

57
00:05:45,980 --> 00:05:52,867
[Slow] 日本銀行は、金利を何%に上げましたか。

58
00:05:53,668 --> 00:05:58,228
[Host] What percent did the Bank of Japan raise its rate to? One percent.

59
00:05:58,827 --> 00:06:04,468
[Slow] なぜ日本銀行は金利を上げましたか。

60
00:06:05,267 --> 00:06:10,067
[Host] Why did the Bank of Japan raise the rate? Because prices have been going up.

61
00:06:10,668 --> 00:06:16,836
[Slow] お金を借りている人は、これからどうなりますか。

62
00:06:17,636 --> 00:06:21,956
[Host] What happens for people who have borrowed money? They have more to pay back.

63
00:06:22,555 --> 00:06:34,939
[Host] That's today's Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

64
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:37,795
[News] また明日。
